  "physical_album_evidence": "The edition documents loose physical leaves from the International and Area Studies Library at the University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign, 19×13.5 inches. The underlying photographs were collected from 1903 and published as phototypes/heliogravures in the period souvenir album.",
  "image_reuse_scope": "Two matched named portrait catalog entries say Public Domain. The colour crop of plate 4 (Baron Freedericksz) has no item-level rights record in the current edition. The historic KIC file listing lacks item-specific rights and hardware metadata. Original dimensions and grayscale files are consistent with a separate flat capture, while the methodology specifically documents separate Epson V850 colour scans for individual portraits. Further confirmation is required before product-use licensing or publication of historic page scans.",
  "registration": "SIFT, descriptor ratio 0.72, cv2.USAC_MAGSAC with 1.4 px estimation after resizing; five-part held-out refit on inliers; errors are upright native page pixels. Registration validates paired artwork and spatial alignment, not corner accuracy, paper ownership, or physical album independence.",
  "reference_caveats": [
    "Outer pale rectangles may be printed collotype reproduction fields. A pigment transition alone does not certify where separately mounted print stock ends.",
    "Some edition crops omit visible grey stock or extend into source margins. Their projected corners are image corners, and cannot be used as verified photograph corners.",
    "Held-out feature p95 is 3.16 to 3.67 native source px depending on the pair. That is larger than the two source-pixel release tolerance and cannot be read as a corner validation.",
    "Full originals are approximately 94–95 MP. A product upload under its default 40 MP cap needs a documented smaller source acquisition or a separate pinned derivative, with reference markings transformed appropriately.",
    "The uncropped p155 leaf has no matching paired reference among the edition files tested.",
    "Complete reuse evidence, human source-only review, independent measured motif/full-print dimensions and model-provenance overlap checks remain required. None of these pages are assigned to training, calibration, or release."
  ],
